    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not even depression really, it just feels... finished. like i spent thirty years running at 100mph and now that i've stopped, there's nothing left to do. i've seen everything i needed to see, done what i was meant to do. it's like being a character in a book where the last chapter is already written and i'm just reading the same page over and over. does that make sense? just existing for the sake of existing?\n volriptide ily ily ily no",
